WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.820
Binding is a security decision because it determines where a service is reachable.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:12.040
A service bound only to a loopback interface has a different exposure profile from a service listening on every interface.

3
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:19.020
A service reachable only inside a private deployment network has a different risk profile from a public-facing endpoint.

4
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.620
Listening on all interfaces can expose a service more broadly than intended.

5
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:35.960
The code may have been tested locally, but deployment can place the same binary on a host with additional network interfaces, container bridges, overlay networks, or routes to other environments.

6
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.180
Binding behavior should match the intended deployment model, not just the developer's workstation.

7
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:51.220
Port choices, service accounts, firewall policy, container networking, orchestration configuration, and load balancer behavior all affect endpoint exposure.

8
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.120
The socket call is only one part of the real boundary.

9
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:59.580
Secure design documents which endpoints are meant to exist and which surrounding controls are required.

10
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.500
Least privilege strengthens the design.

11
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:08.280
The service account should have only the filesystem, process, and network privileges the service needs.

12
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:15.100
If socket logic contains a mistake, a restricted process identity can reduce what the service can affect.

13
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.680
Network exposure and local process privileges should be reviewed together.

14
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.800
Endpoint exposure should be reviewed as part of the application's security boundary.

15
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:36.460
Reviewers should ask which addresses and ports are reachable, who can reach them, which protocol is expected, how access is controlled, and how deployment configuration keeps the service aligned with its intended audience.
